Zakat & Savings Tracker

1. Project Overview

Zakat & Savings Tracker is a mobile application developed using Flutter and Dart. It aims to help users manage their personal assets, monitor savings goals, estimate their zakat obligations, and record zakat payments. The application will use a REST API backend and a relational database to store and manage information.

2. Problem Statement

Managing personal savings, keeping track of assets, and calculating zakat can be difficult when financial information is scattered across notebooks or different applications. Users may struggle to maintain organized financial records, monitor their savings progress, estimate their zakat obligations, and keep track of previous zakat payments.

This project aims to address these challenges by providing one mobile application for organizing assets, savings goals, zakat estimates, and zakat payment records.

3. Proposed Solution

The proposed application will allow registered users to record their assets, create savings goals, estimate zakat based on eligible assets and applicable zakat rules, and record their zakat payments.

A REST API backend will handle communication between the mobile application and the relational database. The system will provide functions for creating, viewing, updating, and deleting records.

4. Project Objectives

- To provide user registration and login.
- To allow users to create, view, update, and delete asset records.
- To enable users to create and monitor savings goals.
- To estimate zakat based on eligible assets and applicable rules.
- To allow users to record and review zakat payments.
- To organize users' financial records in one application.
- To protect users' records through authentication and appropriate access controls.

5. Target Users

The application is intended for individuals who want to organize their personal assets and savings, monitor savings goals, estimate their zakat obligations, and maintain records of zakat payments.

6. Main Features

- User registration and login.
- Personal asset management.
- Savings goal creation and tracking.
- Zakat estimation based on applicable rules.
- Recording and viewing zakat payments.
- Creating, viewing, updating, and deleting supported records.
- Secure access to each user's own records.

7. Proposed Technologies

- Mobile application: Flutter and Dart.
- Backend: REST API.
- Database: Relational database.
- Data exchange format: JSON.
- Version control and collaboration: Git and GitHub.

8. Expected Outcome

The expected outcome is a functional mobile application connected to a backend API and relational database. Users will be able to manage asset records, monitor savings goals, estimate zakat obligations, and record zakat payments through an organized mobile interface.

9. Project Scope

The project will focus on user authentication, asset management, savings goals, zakat estimation, and zakat payment records. The application will include a mobile interface, backend API, and relational database. The implementation will follow the capstone requirements provided by the lecturer.

